50,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"I think Candidate C is the best! They are built for transport and have engineers right here for the rollout, which means they can actually see how the yard works and make it tough enough!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"I cannot support Candidate B. My research shows that separately licensed pieces and add-ons lead to climbing yearly costs, which is exactly the financial trap we must avoid.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Asuka,,I also object to Candidate B. A modular system with separate licenses is a recipe for the fragmented support and finger-pointing I found in the last outage. It lacks a single point of accountability.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I don't like Candidate A! They use a partner firm for the data move, and remember how the 2018 move was a total mess because outsiders did it? We need someone who does it right!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Servas,,"I find Candidate C most promising. Having an engineering team present during the rollout allows for the gentle, tailored transition our stretched staff needs, ensuring the system adapts to the people, not the other way around.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, you're right about the outsiders! Candidate C is way better because the engineers are actually here. They can make sure the system survives the peak season without us having to go back to paper!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Servas, I agree that the presence of an engineering team is a benefit. Furthermore, Candidate C's on-premise model likely avoids the recurring subscription traps and hidden marketplace fees associated with Cloud Suite or modular platforms.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, that is a valid point. Additionally, Candidate C's integrated approach and on-site presence provide the accountability we need. Unlike Candidate D's fixed configuration, C can adapt to depot routines, preventing the operational drift I observed.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, exactly! And since Candidate C is built just for transport, it won't get dusty and old like our dispatch tool. It's like getting a toy that's actually made for playing outside! I really like C!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Servas,,"It is heartening to see such harmony. Candidate C offers a sanctuary for our weary administrators; by having engineers on-site, we reduce the burden on those few who still hold our institutional memory.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm so glad we all agree! Candidate C is the only one that feels like it can actually handle the chaos of the yard and the peak season rush. It's the toughest and smartest choice!,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"Logically, Candidate C is the most sustainable. It avoids the recurring cost traps of A and B, and unlike D, it provides the on-site support necessary to ensure the system is actually adopted by the staff.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"Candidate C is the only option that addresses both of my concerns. The integrated engineering team ensures a single point of accountability, and their on-site presence allows for the flexibility needed to prevent operational drift.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Rin,,"I'm voting for Candidate C! They don't use scary outsiders for the data, and they'll be right here to make sure everything stays shiny and new. It's the best choice for everyone!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Servas,,"I concur. Candidate C is the most compassionate choice, as it provides the hands-on support our people deserve. It is the path of least resistance for our staff and the most secure for our future.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm voting for Candidate C! It's the only one that's tough enough for the yard and won't let us down during the peak season. Let's do this!,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I vote for Candidate C. It is the most fiscally responsible choice, avoiding the hidden recurring costs of subscriptions and modular add-ons while ensuring operational stability through on-site support.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I vote for Candidate C. It is the only vendor that provides the accountability and operational flexibility required to avoid the failures of our previous rollouts.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,4,talk,Rin,,I vote for Candidate C! It's the one that keeps things from getting dusty and doesn't leave us with a broken puzzle. Yay for Candidate C!,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,4,talk,Servas,,"I cast my vote for Candidate C. It is the most mindful selection, ensuring that our remaining experts are supported and our crews are guided with patience. May this transition bring peace and efficiency to all.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
